# dev delivery-system scaffolding (local foreman state — not part of the library)
# `.dev/*` matches only the DIRECT children of .dev, so an ignored directory is
# never descended into and a negation on a file inside it cannot rescue it. Each
# tracked subtree therefore needs its own un-ignore on the directory itself.
# `.dev/hooks/` holds worktree lifecycle hooks: they describe how THIS repo is
# reclaimed, so they are shared, unlike project.sh and plans/ which stay local.
.dev/*
!.dev/checks.sh
!.dev/hooks/

# planning documents are local working state, never shipped in this public repo
docs/plans/
